// HumanityOS Quest Chain: Getting Started
//
// FIRST STEPS IS THE OPENING: a new player's first ten minutes, in the order the
// operator accepted on 2026-10-04 (docs/design/first-hour-audit-2026-10-04.md):
// "check your vitals, eat, plant, craft a tool, send the drone for iron, smelt
// it, build one thing, and end at your front door looking out on the Commons."
// gs_first_steps is accepted on spawn (lib.rs); finishing it accepts Toolsmith,
// and finishing that accepts Build First Habitat (data/quests/tutorial.ron), so
// the HUD's quest line never goes blank between them. A player who finished the
// two-step First Steps of before keeps it finished (the id is unchanged, and a
// finished quest is never accepted again), so nobody is sent back to the start.
//
// Every step is something the game sees the player do, reported where it really
// happens:
//   View(view: "vitals")   the Inventory page's Status section came on screen
//                          (the vitals with their numbers; the HUD's own rows show
//                          only once a need runs low, so a healthy player has none
//                          on screen to look at)
//   Eat(quantity: n)       the food system ate an item from the backpack
//   Plant(quantity: n)     the farming system planted a crop the player sowed
//   Make(item_id, n)       units made by any recipe (crafting reports each one)
//   Gather(item_id, n)     carried, or in home storage (where the drone unloads)
//   Build(blueprint_id)    a piece finished building
//   Travel(destination)    standing in the place while this is the step; the
//                          front door is the player's own, resolved to the plot
//                          they were given (data/entities/destinations.ron)
// Eat and Plant name no item, so any food and any crop count; give them an
// item_id / crop_id to ask for one. A count step counts from when the quest was
// accepted, so doing a later thing early is not wasted; Travel counts only on
// its own step, so passing the door on the way to the forge does not end it.
//
// A step's text is the HUD's quest line, shown as "<text> (1/8)" and cut at 64
// characters (src/gui/pages/hud.rs): it names the key, the page and the section
// as the game shows them. `{front_door_opens_on}` is filled with what the
// player's own front door opens on ("the Commons", "First Street";
// systems::quests::step_text). Each step's completion posts a notice naming the
// next one, and the quest's completion one naming what it gave.
//
// Tests (src/systems/quests/mod.rs, src/machines.rs): the_opening_walks_*
// plays the whole opening on this data with the real systems; every_step_*
// holds every line to the 64 characters and to the places it names;
// every_shipped_home_has_what_the_starter_quests_need checks both shipped homes
// have what each step uses (the station, the food, the seeds, the materials).
//
// Format: Vec<QuestDef>, see src/systems/quests/mod.rs
[
    (
        id: "gs_first_steps",
        name: "First Steps",
        description: "Your first ten minutes aboard: check on yourself, eat, plant, make a tool, bring in iron and smelt it, build something, then step out of your own front door.",
        steps: [
            (
                description: "Check your vitals: press I, see Inventory > Status",
                objective: View(view: "vitals"),
            ),
            (
                description: "Eat something: press I, click a Basic Ration, then Eat",
                objective: Eat(quantity: 1),
            ),
            (
                // The tower design's group, near the top of the Garden section: its
                // button reads "Plant this tower" (or "Plant again" once some cups
                // hold plants), and it sows one seed from the backpack per cup whose
                // plant the player has a seed for (lettuce, tomato, carrot and bean
                // in the starting kit; data/world/player.ron).
                description: "Plant: press I, Garden > Variety Greens and Beans > Plant",
                objective: Plant(quantity: 1),
            ),
            (
                // A fishing rod: the one tool a new home can make before it has
                // metal (a plank and a wire from the Barn, at the workbench).
                description: "Craft a tool: Esc > Crafting > Carve Fishing Rod > Craft",
                objective: Make(item_id: "fishing_rod_0", quantity: 1),
            ),
            (
                // The drone, or the trading post in the vehicle bay: E at it
                // opens its card, whose Trade button opens the shop.
                description: "Get 3 iron ore: Inventory > Mining, or trading post (E)",
                objective: Gather(item_id: "iron_ore_0", quantity: 3),
            ),
            (
                // The smelter burns coal: the starting Barn holds 5 (data/places/seed.json,
                // first-hour audit Friction 4), and the trading post sells more; the
                // graphite a drone brings from asteroid C-3 smelts it too
                // ("Smelt Iron (graphite)"), and either way makes the ingot.
                description: "Smelt iron: Crafting > Smelt Iron (coal is in the Barn)",
                objective: Make(item_id: "iron_ingot_0", quantity: 1),
            ),
            (
                // The Storage Chest, the one chest in the Structures list: eight
                // planks from the Barn, and it holds things once built (E opens it).
                description: "Build a chest: Crafting > Structures > Build, aim, then E",
                objective: Build(blueprint_id: "storage_chest"),
            ),
            (
                description: "Step out your front door and look out on {front_door_opens_on}",
                objective: Travel(destination: "front_door"),
            ),
        ],
        rewards: [
            ("iron_ingot_0", 2),
        ],
        xp_rewards: [
            ("metalworking", 30),
        ],
        prerequisite: None,
    ),
    (
        id: "gs_toolsmith",
        name: "Toolsmith",
        description: "Put your metal to work, forge your first hand tool.",
        steps: [
            (
                // The opening's reward is two iron ingots, one for this.
                description: "Forge a hammer: Esc > Crafting > Craft Hammer > Craft",
                objective: Craft(recipe_id: "craft_hammer", quantity: 1),
            ),
        ],
        rewards: [
            ("wood_plank_0", 4),
        ],
        xp_rewards: [
            ("metalworking", 20),
            ("woodworking", 10),
        ],
        prerequisite: Some("gs_first_steps"),
    ),
]
